<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan CK Group buys 54,000T US corn at tender.</title>
<headline>Taiwan CK Group buys 54,000T US corn at tender.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's CK group bought a 54,000-tonne shipment of U.S. No.2 corn from Mitsui at a tender on Wednesday, traders said.</p>
<p>The CK Group comprises Chia Hsin Flour Feed and Vegetable Oil Corp and some buyers from Taiwan's southern port city of Kaohsiung.  </p>
<p>The shipment's freight was fixed at US$22.48 per tonne from National Shipping Agency Corp, traders said.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follows:</p>
<p>			 U.S. Gulf</p>
<p> Corn  37,500	March 3-15	   US$120.53</p>
<p> Corn  16,500	March 3-15	   38.15 US cents/May</p>
<p>--Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
